{"id":"code-rle-decode","title":"Run-length decoding","category":"code","difficulty":2,"prompt":"Write a Python function `rle_decode(text: str) -> str` that expands a run-length encoded\nstring. The input is a sequence of pairs: a positive decimal count (one or more digits)\nfollowed by a single non-digit character. For example \"3a2b1c\" becomes \"aaabbc\". An empty\ninput gives an empty string.","system":"You are completing one task from an evaluation suite. Do the task as asked.\n\nReply with one Python code block that defines exactly what the task asks for. Use only the standard library. Do not include tests, examples, or print statements.","grader":{"type":"code","entrypoint":"rle_decode","tests":["assert rle_decode(\"\") == \"\"","assert rle_decode(\"3a2b1c\") == \"aaabbc\"","assert rle_decode(\"1a1b\") == \"ab\"","assert rle_decode(\"12x\") == \"x\" * 12","assert rle_decode(\"10a2b\") == \"a\" * 10 + \"bb\"","assert rle_decode(\"2 3-\") == \"  ---\""]},"reference":"```python\ndef rle_decode(text: str) -> str:\n    out = []\n    count = \"\"\n    for ch in text:\n        if ch.isdigit():\n            count += ch\n        else:\n            out.append(ch * int(count))\n            count = \"\"\n    return \"\".join(out)\n```","answers":["```python\ndef rle_decode(text: str) -> str:\n    out = []\n    count = \"\"\n    for ch in text:\n        if ch.isdigit():\n            count += ch\n        else:\n            out.append(ch * int(count))\n            count = \"\"\n    return \"\".join(out)\n```","```python\ndef rle_decode(text: str) -> str:\n    out = []\n    for i in range(0, len(text), 2):\n        out.append(text[i + 1] * int(text[i]))\n    return \"\".join(out)\n```"],"cells":[{"arm":"haiku-low","trial":0,"mode":"batch","status":"ok","score":1.0,"passed":true,"answer":0,"details":{"passed":6,"total":6,"tests":[{"ok":true},{"ok":true},{"ok":true},{"ok":true},{"ok":true},{"ok":true}],"simulated":{"pass_probability":0.838,"answer":"reference"}},"input_tokens"